{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02718",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.75,
      "end_seconds": 4.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.1,
      "end_seconds": 10.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.01,
      "end_seconds": 16.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Well, um, I've been having my heart suddenly racing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.53,
      "end_seconds": 23.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Alright, when did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.8,
      "end_seconds": 37.46,
      "duration_seconds": 12.66,
      "text": "Probably two weeks. Yeah. I've, I've been feeling lightheaded during an episode too. As for feeling lightheaded during an episode, it happens on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.95,
      "end_seconds": 43.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "And what about breathlessness, family history of sudden death or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.36,
      "end_seconds": 52.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "Hmm, I haven't had breathlessness, family history of sudden death or fainting, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.02,
      "end_seconds": 56.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.55,
      "end_seconds": 59.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.05,
      "end_seconds": 72.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.38,
      "end_seconds": 89.69,
      "duration_seconds": 15.31,
      "text": "Hmm, just keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.22,
      "end_seconds": 93.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.88,
      "end_seconds": 99.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Trimethoprim. I come out in... well, itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.31,
      "end_seconds": 103.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.19,
      "end_seconds": 108.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.27,
      "end_seconds": 113.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.11,
      "end_seconds": 119.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.6,
      "end_seconds": 125.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.46,
      "end_seconds": 131.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "I've, I've had asthma for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.31,
      "end_seconds": 136.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Okay, I can see asthma in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.98,
      "end_seconds": 147.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.84,
      "end_seconds": 161.28,
      "duration_seconds": 13.44,
      "text": "I take Foracort inhaler, twice a day. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.81,
      "end_seconds": 183.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Alright, time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.39,
      "end_seconds": 197.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.37,
      "end_seconds": 220.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.82,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 114 over 80, saturation 97 percent, heart rate 81, temp 36.6 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.78,
      "end_seconds": 226.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.96,
      "end_seconds": 241.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.9,
      "end_seconds": 245.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.98,
      "end_seconds": 261.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Your heart sounds and rhythm are normal today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.72,
      "end_seconds": 281.36,
      "duration_seconds": 15.64,
      "text": "You can relax now. Let me tell you where I've got to. I think we're dealing with episodes of supraventricular tachycardia at this stage. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.44,
      "end_seconds": 285.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.97,
      "end_seconds": 322.92,
      "duration_seconds": 31.95,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like episodes of supraventricular tachycardia, but I'd like to confirm. I'll request a thyroid test, it'll help with palpitations. Try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts. We'll refer you to the cardiology clinic. I'm not ordering an ECG today. If things carry on next month, we'll consider it. See me again after the monitor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.92,
      "end_seconds": 327.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Alright, I'll be back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.86,
      "end_seconds": 331.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "So, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.93,
      "end_seconds": 336.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Erm, thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}